This project is a Claude Code adaptation of the selective-routing workflow introduced
by Sol Advisor (https://github.com/DannyMac180/sol-advisor), Copyright (c) 2026
Daniel McAteer, also MIT licensed. The route grammar, the four delivery modes, the
single-auxiliary maximum, and the five-part worker specification originate there.

It is an adaptation rather than an independent implementation: the canonical workflow
was written by working through the original section by section, and a substantial
portion of its prose is derived from that text, including some identical sentences.
No file was copied. The agent definitions, the Claude lane pins, the chair/floor
mechanism, and the enforcement properties described in the README are new work.

ORIGIN.md states the extent of the overlap in detail, measured at the sentence level.
Where these two files appear to disagree, ORIGIN.md is correct.

